WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.499
Academia and industry have built several
privacy-preserving strategies,

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:05.789
but each has limits.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:11.401
Encryption approaches like homomorphic encryption
offer strong security yet are hard to

00:00:11.481 --> 00:00:15.594
deploy in real settings because of their technology
requirements.

00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:19.270
Federated learning decentralizes training across devices,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:23.205
but it assumes every peer holds the same kind of
information,

00:00:23.285 --> 00:00:27.397
so it cannot handle two peers that contribute
different features.

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:31.332
Differential privacy masks individual values by
adding noise,

00:00:31.412 --> 00:00:34.169
which can significantly reduce data utility.

00:00:34.249 --> 00:00:39.846
Linear dimensionality reduction such as Principal
Component Analysis obfuscates features

00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:42.877
but may lose important nonlinear relationships.

00:00:42.957 --> 00:00:48.553
These gaps motivate a new approach that uses deep
representation learning to encode data

00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:51.520
while keeping its predictive structure intact.
